Database migrations (Alembic)
=============================

The schema is defined by the SQLModel models in `src/models/` and applied
to the database through the revisions in `versions/`. Nothing creates
tables at application startup.

`migrations/env.py` takes the database URL from
`src.core.config.settings.DATABASE_URL` and the target metadata from
`SQLModel.metadata`, so `alembic` uses the same configuration as the app.
Run it from the project root with the environment loaded (the `.env`
file, or exported variables):

    alembic upgrade head              # apply all pending migrations
    alembic downgrade -1              # roll back the last one
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
    alembic check                     # fail if models drift from migrations

`alembic revision --autogenerate` and `alembic check` compare against the
*live* database, so point `DATABASE_URL` at a real PostgreSQL instance
(e.g. the `docker compose` one). Running them against SQLite reports
spurious `server_default` diffs because SQLite stores `now()` as
`CURRENT_TIMESTAMP`.

First-time adoption on a database that predates Alembic (its tables were
created by the old `create_all` startup hook):

    alembic stamp head               # record head without running the migration

then apply anything added since by hand — currently the
`song_links (song_id, platform)` unique constraint:

    ALTER TABLE song_links ADD CONSTRAINT uq_song_links_song_id_platform
        UNIQUE (song_id, platform);
